Acknowledgements
----------------

Two features of this fork were inspired by other open-source converters. The
ideas were reimplemented on top of this project's own handlers; no code was
taken from either.

VERT (AGPL-3.0)          https://github.com/VERT-sh/VERT
  Per-conversion output settings.
CompressZ (Apache-2.0)   https://github.com/ADJ189/CompressZ
  Two-pass GIF palette generation, and bundling several outputs in one zip.

Third-party code and data added by this fork
--------------------------------------------

zip.js (BSD-3-Clause), Gildas Lormeau   https://github.com/gildas-lormeau/zip.js
  Bundling several outputs in one zip, with optional AES encryption.
SVGO (MIT)                              https://github.com/svg/svgo
html-minifier-terser (MIT)              https://github.com/terser/html-minifier-terser
terser (BSD-2-Clause)                   https://github.com/terser/terser
  Minifying SVG, HTML and JavaScript when a file is converted to its own format.
Arachnidium (MIT), p2r3                 https://github.com/p2r3/Arachnidium
  The idea of minifying web formats and of keeping the original when the
  result is not smaller. Reimplemented here; no code was taken.
ONNX Runtime Web (MIT), Microsoft       https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime
U2-Net "u2netp" model (Apache-2.0), Xuebin Qin et al.
                                        https://github.com/xuebinqin/U-2-Net
  Background removal. The model file is fetched at build time from the rembg
  releases (https://github.com/danielgatis/rembg), see recipe/requirements.config.ts.
tesseract.js and tesseract.js-core (Apache-2.0), naptha
                                        https://github.com/naptha/tesseract.js
Tesseract OCR and its language data (Apache-2.0)
                                        https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tesseract
  Text recognition (English and Dutch).

Merging PDFs, resizing, trimming and removing metadata use libraries the
project already had: mupdf, ImageMagick, FFmpeg and mediabunny.

Licensing notes
---------------

These concern the upstream project as much as this fork, and are recorded
here so that anyone redistributing a build knows about them. They are not
legal advice.

The upstream repository carries the text of GPL version 2 and does not say
whether it means "version 2 only" or "version 2 or any later version". That
matters, because some of the libraries a build bundles have licences that the
Free Software Foundation considers incompatible with GPL version 2 on its own,
and compatible with GPL version 3:

  mupdf                        AGPL-3.0-or-later
  pdfjs-dist                   Apache-2.0
  @imagemagick/magick-wasm     Apache-2.0
  @sqlite.org/sqlite-wasm      Apache-2.0
  @myriaddreamin/typst.ts      Apache-2.0 (with its renderer and compiler)
  @aiden0z/pptx-renderer       Apache-2.0
  bson, comlink, less, pdf-parse, wabt    Apache-2.0
  tesseract.js, tesseract.js-core        Apache-2.0 (added by this fork)
  U2-Net "u2netp" model weights          Apache-2.0 (added by this fork)

@ffmpeg/core is GPL-2.0-or-later. The mediabunny packages are MPL-2.0, which
can be combined with the GPL. The remaining dependencies are under MIT, ISC,
BSD, OFL or similarly permissive licences.

Which version of the GPL applies to the project is for its copyright holders
to say. This fork does not change LICENSE and does not claim to settle the
question. A build that includes mupdf also has to meet the terms of the
AGPL for that library.

Each dependency's own licence text is in its package under node_modules/
after `bun install`.
